{
 "_": [
  "FILM 7 -- The Goose Who Gave Gold (jataka-more).",
  "",
  "THE PRIMITIVE IS `count`: a set a child can count, that changes. docs/03 named the two",
  "embarrassing outcomes exactly -- the feathers not matching the number of visits, and the",
  "goose after the grab reading as a SECOND goose -- and both are solved the same way, which",
  "is the `carry` lesson at its smallest. THE GOLD FEATHER AND THE WHITE ONE ARE THE SAME PNG.",
  "The gold ones carry a gild filter; the plain ones do not. 'Every single one of them turned",
  "into an ordinary white feather' is then literally true of the pixels, and the golden goose",
  "and the plain goose are one drawing too, so he cannot come back as a different bird.",
  "",
  "rig.count owns the size, the spacing and the SPOTS -- a shot picks a declared spot by name",
  "and says how many of each colour. There is no field for moving a feather. film.js then",
  "checks the arithmetic across the whole film: the total never goes down, gold never comes",
  "back once anything has turned, the total is FIXED once it has turned (the girls kept all",
  "of them and no new ones appeared), and both states are on screen.",
  "",
  "EDITORIAL. The mother is not a villain and the film must not play her as one -- see",
  "cast/mother/cast.json. There is no snatching, no bird in anyone's hands and no plucked",
  "goose in any shot: she kneels and reaches with open hands, and the next picture is six",
  "white feathers. The colour change IS the event, which is as elliptical as the app's own",
  "telling. Never braver than the text."
 ],
